text:
Sec.  1-6.  Certain ordinances not affected by Code.
Nothing in this Code or the ordinance adopting this Code shall be construed to repeal or otherwise affect the validity of any of the following:
a. Any ordinance promising or guaranteeing the payment of money for the city, or authorizing the issuance of  any bonds of  the city or any evidence of the city's indebtedness;
b. Any administrative ordinances not in conflict or inconsistent with the provisions of this Code;
c. Any appropriation ordinance or ordinance providing for the levy of  taxes or for an annual budget, or any amendment thereto;
d. Any ordinance annexing territory to the city or excluding territory as a part of the city;
e. Any ordinance granting any franchise, permit or other right;
f. Any ordinance dedicating, naming, establishing, locating, relocating, opening, closing, paving, widening, vacating or establishing grades of any street or public way in the city;
g. Any  ordinance  providing  for  local  improvements or relating to special assessments therefor;
h. Any  ordinance  dedicating  or  accepting  any plat or subdivision in the city;
i. Any ordinance approving, authorizing or otherwise relating to any contract, agreement, lease, deed or other instrument;
j. Any  ordinance  zoning  or  rezoning  specific property in the city as to zoning classification;
k. Reserved;
l. Any temporary or special ordinance;
and all such ordinances are hereby recognized as continuing in full force and effect to the same extent as if set out at length herein. Each of the above-mentioned ordinances shall in no way be repealed except as the same  may  be  in  conflict  with  the  provisions  of  this Code.
(Code 1983, § 1-6)

